   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Let F be the antiderivative of \\( f(x) = \\frac{x}{\\left(x^{2} + 1\\right)^{2}} \\) with \\( F(1) = 1 \\). Find the exact value of \\( F\\left(2\\right) \\)."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Rational",
         23,
         20
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Let \\( u = x^{2} + 1 \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            [
               "Power",
               "x",
               2
            ],
            1
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Then \\( du = 2 x \\, dx \\), so \\( x \\, dx = \\frac{1}{2} \\, du \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            1,
            2
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Since \\( F(2) = F(1) + \\int_{1}^{2} \\frac{x}{\\left(x^{2} + 1\\right)^{2}} \\, dx \\), convert the limits: \\( x = 1 \\) gives \\( u = 2 \\) and \\( x = 2 \\) gives \\( u = 5 \\), so the integral becomes \\( \\int_{2}^{5} \\frac{1}{2 u^{2}} \\, du \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            1,
            [
               "Multiply",
               2,
               [
                  "Power",
                  "u",
                  2
               ]
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "An antiderivative of \\( \\frac{1}{2 u^{2}} \\) is \\( - \\frac{1}{2 u} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Negate",
            [
               "Divide",
               1,
               [
                  "Multiply",
                  2,
                  "u"
               ]
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 5,
         "text": "The integral is \\( - \\frac{1}{10} - \\left(- \\frac{1}{4}\\right) = \\frac{3}{20} \\), so \\( F(2) = 1 + \\frac{3}{20} = \\frac{23}{20} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            23,
            20
         ]
      }
   ],
